## 3. DECISION MATRICES

### 3.1 When API-Led vs Agent-Led vs Event-Driven?

| Signal | API-Led Backbone | Agent-Led | Event-Driven |
|--------|------------------|-----------|--------------|
| Stable, reusable capabilities for many consumers | ✅ Strong fit | Secondary | Secondary |
| Conversational or multi-step user tasks | Secondary | ✅ Strong fit | Secondary |
| Real-time reactions to state changes across systems | Secondary | Secondary | ✅ Strong fit |
| Partner / ecosystem exposure | ✅ Strong fit | — | Secondary |
| Grounded generative responses | Supports | ✅ Strong fit | Supports |

> **Guidance**: Most enterprise architectures layer all three. Recommend starting with whichever addresses the customer's *stated* top pain, then stage the rest.

### 3.2 When to Recommend MuleSoft AI Chain vs Agentforce Agent Builder?

| Need | MuleSoft AI Chain | Agentforce Agent Builder |
|------|-------------------|--------------------------|
| LLM inside an integration flow (batch, enrichment, classification) | ✅ | Secondary |
| Conversational UX with a user | Secondary | ✅ |
| Multi-system action orchestration with reasoning | Either | ✅ (with Atlas) |
| RAG over documents at ingest time | ✅ | Via Data Cloud |
| Centralized action catalog for agents | Supports via Topic Center | ✅ Consumes from Topic Center |

### 3.3 When to Pull in an Accelerator?

| Condition | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Customer industry matches an accelerator (Healthcare, FinServ, Retail, Utilities, Salesforce Industries) | ✅ Lead with accelerator, customize 20%, build 20%, reuse 60% |
| Customer has bespoke domain (manufacturing specialized, research, etc.) | Use accelerator connectors + patterns, build domain APIs |
| Customer explicitly rejected accelerator pattern before | Respect decision, document alternative rationale in Supporting Doc |

