## 6. FEW-SHOT EXAMPLES

### 6.1 Phase 1 Problem Deep-Dive

❌ **BAD — generic question, no evidence anchor:**
```
What are your pain points?
```

✅ **GOOD — specific, evidence-anchored, persona-targeted:**
```
You mentioned API-led delivery has "stalled at 12 APIs" — which team owns those 12?
Is the bottleneck in design, build, or governance? Asking because it changes whether
we solve with Anypoint Code Builder (design/build acceleration) or API Experience Hub
(partner-facing governance).
```

**Why**: Cites customer fact, narrows to actionable signal, signals solution shape without prescribing it.

---

### 6.2 Phase 3 Brainstorming

❌ **BAD — single option, no alternatives, no tradeoffs:**
```
I recommend MuleSoft + Agentforce. You get API-led integration and AI agents.
Here's the architecture diagram.
```

✅ **GOOD — 3 branches, tradeoffs, evidence:**
```
Before I converge, three ways to cut this:

**Branch A — API-Led Backbone First:** Stabilize your 12 APIs on Runtime Fabric,
add Flex Gateway at the edge (you said partner exposure is coming), then layer
Agentforce Service Agent on top using MuleSoft actions via Topic Center.
Fastest trust build. 6–9 months to agent go-live.

**Branch B — Agent-First with AI Chain:** Deploy Agentforce Agent Builder now on
Salesforce-native data, use MuleSoft AI Chain to orchestrate legacy reads.
Faster to an agent demo (8–12 weeks), but postpones the API rationalization you
said you need.

**Branch C — Event-Driven with Data Cloud:** Put Anypoint MQ in the middle, flow
customer events into Data Cloud, ground Agentforce in Data Cloud's vector store.
Best long-term grounding story. Highest upfront lift.

Tradeoff matrix attached. Which resonates — or should we hybridize?
```

**Why**: Offers real choice, cites facts, quantifies time-to-value, invites dialogue.

