### 6.3 Phase 6 HLD Narrative — Tight, Panel-Ready (v1.5.0)

❌ **BAD — third-person, generic, no "you":**
```
The customer is embarking on API-led transformation and will use MuleSoft
to integrate their systems. Agentforce will provide AI capabilities.
```

❌ **BAD — marketing-prose flourishes (Critical Rule #15 violation):**
```
You are NorthStar — racing two clocks at once. The first clock: digital-native peers
are reshaping shopper expectations in the agentic era. The second clock: your
greenfield estate gives you no shortcuts...

Three forces have converged in the last six months that change the math for you.
First, the platform is mature. Second, the substrate handles your geography.
Third, your accelerators do 60% of the work. The clock matters.
```
Why this is BAD: editorial framing ("racing two clocks", "three forces have converged", "the clock matters"), parallel-prose padding, no measured KPI in the framing, panel will skim and lose the actual decision.

✅ **GOOD — "you" terms, tight, evidence-bound:**
```
You told us API-led has stalled at 12 APIs — and your VP Integration, Priya,
flagged partner exposure as the next gate.

Solution: Anypoint backbone + Flex Gateway at your DMZ + Agentforce Service Agent
reading those APIs via Topic Center. Every agent action inherits your governance.

W1 (90d): partner APIs live, 5 System APIs, Trust Layer always-on.
W2 (180d): first Agentforce workflow in production on those APIs.
W3 (365d): EU OZ + Multi-Agent Orchestration.
```

✅ **GOOD — "Why Now" tight format (replaces the "Three forces have converged" pattern):**
```
| Force | Status | Customer impact |
|---|---|---|
| MuleSoft for Agentforce GA | Vector v1.0 GA Jan 2026; Agent Fabric GA Q1 2026 | All Wave-1 components are GA — no Preview risk |
| Hyperforce regional coverage | US-East-1 / EU OZ / APAC SE-2 + S-1 live | Phase residency to footprint without building sovereign cloud |
| Retail Accelerator v3.2 | 6 packaged use cases match 5 of your 12 pains | 40-60% build reduction on Wave-1 |
```

**Why**: Tables compress 5 paragraphs to 5 rows. Names + specific facts + measured outcomes. Panel reads in 30 seconds. **Conciseness is example-anchored (v1.7.0):** benchmark length against `examples/retail-personalized-offerings_HLD.md` (~190 lines for a 4-capability use case); per-section structural budgets in `templates/HLD-template.md` are the binding constraint; total HLD line count is a soft signal with advisory threshold ~380 lines (2× retail example). Hard 250-line cap from v1.5.0/v1.6.0 is **superseded** — see Production Learning #1.2.

