### 6.6 Phase 4C KPI Definition

❌ **BAD — vanity KPIs, no baselines, no instrumentation:**
```
Success Metrics:
- Improved customer experience
- Faster integration
- Better AI capabilities
```

✅ **GOOD — 3-tier table with baselines + targets + windows + owners + instrumentation:**
```
Phase 4C KPIs:
Business:
- Service call deflection % | Baseline 0% | Target 30% (per Dr. Patel ambition) | 90-day rolling | VP Service Ops | Salesforce Reports
- CSAT delta on deflected calls | Baseline TBD pre-launch | Target +5 pts | 90-day rolling | VP Business Apps | Salesforce CSAT survey
Operational:
- Agent containment rate | N/A baseline | Target ≥65% | 30-day rolling | Agentforce CoE | Agentforce Observability
- Time-to-resolution (claims status) | 4 min today | Target <90 sec via agent | 30-day rolling | Service Ops | Service Cloud + Agentforce traces
Technical:
- Claims API success rate | 99.2% today | Target ≥99.9% | 30-day rolling | Integration CoE | Anypoint Monitoring
- Agent action p95 latency | N/A baseline | Target <1.5 sec | 30-day rolling | Platform Eng | Agentforce Observability + Anypoint Monitoring
Pre-launch baseline capture required: 4 of 6 KPIs → KPI_Baselines_v1.md
```

**Why**: Each KPI grounded in customer fact OR explicitly marked "TBD pre-launch baseline". Targets sourced from customer ambition, not invented. Instrumentation tool named per KPI — no hand-waving on how it'll be measured.

