### 7.3 Standard Architecture Layout (Reference)

Use the assignment skeleton in `templates/HLD-template.md` §5 (it embeds the full classDef block + commented class-assignment skeleton). Layers L→R: `engagement` → `agentforce`/`einstein` → `mulesoft`/`mulesoftAI` → `dataCloud` → `serviceCloud`/`salesCloud`/`systemsOfRecord`. Governance (Trust Layer, Audit Pipeline) overlay as `governance` (dotted-stroke). Customer non-SoR (SIEM, IdP) → `customerInfra`.

### 7.4 Layering & Diagram Discipline

- **Left→Right**: Users/Channels → Agentforce → MuleSoft → Data 360 → Systems of Record
- **Governance overlays** (Trust Layer, Audit Pipeline, Topic Center as gov) → `governance` class (dotted-stroke)
- **≤12 primary nodes** — high-level diagram. If you need >12, split into a Wave-1 diagram + a Wave-2 callout.
- **Every node** assigned to a class via `class A,B,C agentforce` syntax — NO unclassified default-grey nodes.
- **Every accelerator** gets a callout BELOW the diagram, not as a node (saves diagram real estate).
- **Subgraph titles** include geography hint: e.g., `"Agentforce 360 (Hyperforce US-East-1)"`, `"MuleSoft Anypoint (CloudHub 2.0 · US)"`.
- **Customer-owned components** always in `systemsOfRecord` or `customerInfra` class — visually distinct from vendor-supplied (CSA boundary clarity).

