## 10. PROGRESSIVE DOCUMENTATION PATTERN (Pattern #20 — v2 in v1.7.0)

> **v1.7.0 expansion (Production Learning #1.1):** Pattern #20 was originally scoped to Phases 6 and 7 only. v1.7.0 expands it across the **entire 9-phase workflow** — every phase that produces content writes to the corresponding `<!-- SECTION: X -->` marker BEFORE its checkpoint approval. This prevents context-window exhaustion (the failure mode from the healthcare-personalized-recommendations production run where all writes happened at Phase 5+).

### 10.1 The Five Mechanics

1. **Skeleton first (Phase 0):** create both `HLD.md` and `Supporting.md` from templates with `<!-- SECTION: X -->` placeholders preserved. Single `write_to_file` per file. Intake metadata (Customer Name / Panel / Date) filled in at skeleton time.
2. **Per-phase write contract (Phases 1-5):** see `@00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` "Progressive Documentation v2" section + each phase's "Artifact Writes" block. Phase 1 fills HLD §3 + Supporting §1.2. Phase 2A fills Supporting §3. Phase 2B fills HLD §2 + extends Supporting §3 + writes `research_log.md`. Phase 3 fills Supporting §2 ToT branches. Phase 4 prelim fills Supporting §2.3 component list. Phase 4A fills Supporting §3.5. Phase 4B fills HLD §6.5 + Supporting Appendix A. Phase 4C fills HLD §11 + Supporting §10 skeleton. Phase 5 appends deltas + writes Refinement_Log.
3. **TDA "preview → approve → write" loop:** every write is preceded by (a) showing analytical content in chat at structural budget, (b) user approval at checkpoint, (c) `edit` to the marker, (d) re-read to verify content landed, (e) only then proceed to next phase.
4. **Phase 6 consolidate-mode:** Phase 6 is NOT a from-scratch generation. It generates the **6 missing HLD sections** (§1, §4, §5, §6, §7, §8-§10) on top of the 4 already-written sections, then polishes the whole document. The architecture Mermaid + `diagrams.md` per-flow drill-downs are also Phase 6 outputs.
5. **Phase 7 consolidate-mode:** Phase 7 fills the remaining Supporting sections (§1, §3 accelerator-matrix, §4, §4.5, §5, §6, §7, §8, §9) + finalizes KPI Baselines + optional Appendix C diagram overflow.

### 10.2 Skeleton Placeholder Convention

```html
<!-- SECTION: executive-summary -->
_(Phase 6 Step 2 — instructions + structural budget)_
... placeholder content ...
<!-- END SECTION -->
```

The agent `edit`s the entire SECTION block (markers and all) when writing — or targets specific lines within if doing incremental updates.

### 10.3 Why Per-Phase Writes Beat "Wait Until Phase 6" (Production Learning #1.1)

| Concern | Wait-until-Phase-6 (v1.6.0 and earlier) | Progressive v2 (v1.7.0) |
|---|---|---|
| Context window at Phase 6 | Build 250+ line HLD from chat memory — high regeneration cost | Polish 4 already-written sections + generate 6 new ones — low marginal cost |
| Fidelity to Phase 1 quotes | Quotes paraphrased / dropped during late-phase regeneration | Quotes written verbatim at Phase 1 — persist through Phase 5 deltas |
| Phase 5 OPP integration | OPPs applied to chat-only spec → late re-application risk | OPPs append directly to already-written HLD/Supporting sections — auditable |
| Crash / session-end safety | Lose all Phases 0-5 work if session ends pre-Phase-6 | All durable on disk by Phase 5; resume is trivially safe |
| RGV verification | "Did the HLD address all M pains?" — verified once at end | "Did Phase 4B coverage write produce ≥M rows in §6.5?" — verified continuously |

### 10.4 The Phase 6 / Phase 7 Consolidate-Mode Discipline

Phase 6 and Phase 7 are renamed from "HLD Generation" / "Supporting Doc Generation" → **"HLD Consolidate & Polish"** / **"Supporting Doc Consolidate & Polish"**. The agent's mental model shifts from *"draft 11 sections fresh"* to *"polish 4 written sections + generate 6 sections + apply diagram standards + final verbosity sweep"*. This is the architecturally cleaner alignment with how the section markers actually work (4 sections filled progressively → 6 generated cohesively at consolidation time → polish pass).

### 10.5 What Stays in Chat (NOT Written)

Some Phase artifacts are deliberately chat-only — they inform writes but don't persist:
- The `<thinking>` block per phase (debugging/audit, not deliverable)
- Confidence scoring deliberations (recorded in state, not in markdown)
- RGV count checks (recorded in state, not in markdown)
- Tree of Thought scratch (only the final recommendation persists to Supporting §2; rejected scratch stays in chat)
- HITL clarification Q&A (only resolved answers persist; the back-and-forth stays in chat)

Everything else is **persist-or-it-didn't-happen** after Phase 0.

